{"course": {"id": "s19", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Lower Secondary Mathematics — Stage 9", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "Number and Calculation"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Expressions and Formulae"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Decimals, Percentages and Rounding"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Equations and Inequalities"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 6, "t": "Statistical Investigations"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Shapes and Measurements"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Fractions"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Sequences and Functions"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Graphs"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Position and Transformation"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Volume, Surface Area and Symmetry"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Interpreting and Discussing Results"}]}, "unit": {"n": 11, "stage": 19, "title": "Ratio and proportion", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Simplifying and sharing in ratios, comparing ratios, and solving direct and inverse proportion problems.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Lower Secondary Mathematics (0862), Stage 9", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m9u11.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"sec": "11.1", "code": "9Nf.07", "codeNote": "", "t": "Use ratios: simplify, share an amount in a ratio, and solve problems where one share or the difference is known."}, "O2": {"sec": "11.2", "code": "9Nf.08", "codeNote": "", "t": "Recognise and solve problems involving direct and inverse proportion, including best-value comparisons."}}, "sections": [{"id": "11.1", "title": "Using ratios", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Prize money", "p": ["Three team members share prize money in the ratio **3 : 4 : 8**, based on hours worked. The smallest share is **$45**.", "How much was the total prize? How much more did the top earner get than the middle one? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Sharing in a ratio", "p": ["Share $120 in 4 : 5 : 6 → 15 parts, $8 each → $32, $40, $48."], "qq": {"id": "m9u11s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Share 90 in 2 : 7. Larger part?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 70, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "70."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Working backwards from one share", "p": ["The smallest share, $45, is **3 parts**, so 1 part = $15."], "table": {"head": ["Person", "Parts", "Share"], "rows": [["A", "3", "$45"], ["B", "4", "$60"], ["C", "8", "$120"], ["Total", "15", "$225"]]}, "p2": ["Top earner gets $120 − $60 = **$60** more than the middle one."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Ratios in many contexts", "p": ["Ratios appear in recipes, maps (1 : 50 000), mixtures, gear teeth, exchange rates and similar shapes.", "When the ratio **changes** (people added, money spent), work with the actual amounts, then form the new ratio.", "Ratio and fractions: in 3 : 4 : 8, A gets 3/15 = 1/5 of the total."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Total", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m9u11s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 2 : 5. The larger share is $35. Total ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 49, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "5 parts = 35.", "reason": "49."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I solve ratio problems?", "p": ["Step 1: Write the ratio and the total number of parts.", "Step 2: Use the given information (total, one share, or a difference) to find 1 part.", "Step 3: Multiply to find the quantities needed.", "Step 4: Check the shares match all the facts."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Difference", "p": [], "q": "Ratio 5 : 2. The difference between the shares is 27. Total?", "steps": [["3 parts = 27 → 1 part = 9", ""], ["7 parts = 63", ""]], "a": "63"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Changing ratio", "p": [], "q": "Boys : girls = 3 : 5 in a club of 40. 4 boys join. New ratio?", "steps": [["boys 15, girls 25", ""], ["19 : 25", ""]], "a": "19 : 25"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Fraction of a whole", "p": [], "q": "Cement : sand : gravel = 1 : 2 : 5. What fraction is sand?", "steps": [["2 of 8 parts", ""]], "a": "1/4"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Map ratio", "p": [], "q": "Map 1 : 25 000. 6.4 cm on the map is how many km?", "steps": [["6.4 × 25 000 = 160 000 cm", ""], ["= 1.6 km", ""]], "a": "1.6 km"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Middle share", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m9u11s1t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 2 : 3 : 7, largest share 84. Middle share?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 36, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "1 part = 12.", "reason": "36."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Divided by the wrong number", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Ratio 3 : 4 : 8. A's share (3 parts) is $45. Total?", "lines": ["45 ÷ 15 = 3 per part", "total 3 × 15 = 45"], "bad": 0, "why": "$45 is 3 parts, not the total: 1 part = 45 ÷ 3 = $15, total 15 × 15 = $225.", "fix": [["1 part = $15", ""], ["total $225", ""]], "id": "m9u11s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Treating one share as the total", "p": ["Read carefully which quantity you are given."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Business partners split profits in ratio of investment; maps and models use scale ratios."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Find the value of one part first.", "Use total, share or difference.", "Recalculate actual amounts when a ratio changes.", "Ratios ↔ fractions of the total."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 720, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "11.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: total prize ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 225, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "11.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s1k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "B's share ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 60, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "11.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s1k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 5 : 2, difference 27. Total?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 63, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "11.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s1k04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Quick check: in 1 : 2 : 5, gravel's fraction is …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "5/8", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "5/7", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 436]], "req": [{"id": "m9u11s1r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 3 : 5, smaller share 24. Total?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 64, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 1 : 4 : 5, total 200. Largest?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 100, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 7 : 3, difference 20. Larger?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 35, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1r04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 2 : 9, larger 54. Smaller?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1r05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Fraction of the whole for '3' in 3 : 7?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "3/10", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "3/7", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m9u11s1r06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Map 1 : 50 000. 4 cm = ? km", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1r07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 4 : 5 : 6; middle share $40. Total ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1r08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Squash : water = 1 : 6. Squash in 1.4 L of drink (L)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "prac": [{"id": "m9u11s1p01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 3 : 8. The larger share is $65 more than the smaller. Total ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 143, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "5 parts = 65.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1p02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Red : blue = 2 : 3 with 30 counters. 6 red are removed. New ratio?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1 : 3", "ok": true, "fb": "6 : 18."}, {"t": "2 : 3", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m9u11s1p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Angles of a quadrilateral in the ratio 2 : 3 : 3 : 4. Largest?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1p04", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain how to find the total when you know the middle share of a 2 : 5 : 9 ratio is $75.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "75 ÷ 5 = 15 per part", "kw": ["15|÷ ?5"]}, {"pt": "× 16 parts = 240", "kw": ["16|240"]}], "need": 2, "model": "The middle share is 5 parts, so 1 part = $15; there are 16 parts, so the total is $240.", "hint": "", "reason": "The middle share is 5 parts, so 1 part = $15; there are 16 parts, so the total is $240."}, {"id": "m9u11s1p05", "type": "num", "prompt": "A model car is 1 : 43. Real car 4.3 m. Model length (cm)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1p06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio a : b = 3 : 5 and b : c = 2 : 3. Find c if a = 12.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 30, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "a : b : c = 6 : 10 : 15.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1p07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Profit shared 5 : 3. The larger share is $600. Profit ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 960, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1p08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Gear A 36 teeth, gear B 12 teeth. Ratio of turns A : B?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1 : 3", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "3 : 1", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "adv": [{"id": "m9u11s1a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Boys : girls is 4 : 5. After 6 girls leave it is 1 : 1. Boys?", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 24, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "5x − 6 = 4x.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. $x is shared 3 : 7. If it were shared 1 : 1, the first person would get $24 more. x?", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "x/2 − 3x/10 = 24.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1a03", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. Is the ratio 3 : 5 the same as 6 : 8? Explain.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "no", "kw": ["\\bno\\b|not"]}, {"pt": "3:5 = 6:10 / different fractions", "kw": ["10|0\\.6|0\\.75|3/8|6/14|fraction"]}], "need": 2, "model": "No: doubling 3 : 5 gives 6 : 10, not 6 : 8 (3/5 = 0.6 but 6/8 = 0.75).", "hint": "", "reason": "No: doubling 3 : 5 gives 6 : 10, not 6 : 8 (3/5 = 0.6 but 6/8 = 0.75)."}], "more": [{"id": "m9u11s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Share 30 in 1 : 2. Larger?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 20, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 1 : 3, smaller 5. Total?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 20, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 2 : 1, difference 4. Total?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 1 : 1 : 2, total 40. Largest?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 20, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Map 1 : 1000. 5 cm = ? m", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 50, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s1m06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "In 1 : 4, fraction of the first?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1/5", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1/4", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c9u11", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 11.1 notes · Using ratios", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "11.2", "title": "Direct and inverse proportion", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Painting the hall", "p": ["**4 painters** take **6 days** to paint a school hall. The head teacher wants it done faster and hires more painters.", "With 8 painters, how long? Does 'more painters' mean 'more days' as in a recipe? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Direct proportion", "p": ["3 kg cost $7.50 → 1 kg $2.50 → 5 kg $12.50."], "qq": {"id": "m9u11s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "6 tickets cost $45. Cost of 10 ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 75, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "75."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Inverse proportion", "p": ["Two quantities are in **inverse proportion** when one increases and the other decreases **in the same ratio**: double one → halve the other.", "Their **product is constant**: painters × days = 4 × 6 = **24 painter-days**."], "table": {"head": ["Painters", "2", "4", "6", "8", "12"], "rows": [["Days", "12", "6", "4", "3", "2"]]}, "p2": ["8 painters: 24 ÷ 8 = **3 days** (assuming they all work at the same rate)."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Which kind?", "p": ["**Direct**: the ratio y : x stays the same (cost and number of items, distance and fuel). Divide to find the rate.", "**Inverse**: the product x × y stays the same (workers and time for a job, speed and time for a fixed journey). Multiply to find the total.", "Ask: 'if one doubles, does the other double or halve?'"]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Inverse", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m9u11s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "3 pumps empty a tank in 8 hours. How long for 6 pumps?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "3 × 8 = 24 pump-hours.", "reason": "4 hours."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I solve proportion problems?", "p": ["Step 1: Decide: direct or inverse?", "Step 2: Direct: find the amount for 1 unit (divide), then multiply.", "Step 3: Inverse: find the constant product (multiply), then divide.", "Step 4: Check the answer makes sense (more workers → less time)."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Speed and time", "p": [], "q": "At 60 km/h a trip takes 2 hours. At 80 km/h?", "steps": [["distance = 120 km (constant)", ""], ["120 ÷ 80 = 1.5", ""]], "a": "1.5 hours"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Food supplies", "p": [], "q": "Food for 30 campers lasts 12 days. How long for 40 campers?", "steps": [["30 × 12 = 360 camper-days", ""], ["360 ÷ 40 = 9", ""]], "a": "9 days"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Direct", "p": [], "q": "A printer prints 42 pages in 3 minutes. Pages in 8 minutes?", "steps": [["14 per minute", ""], ["112", ""]], "a": "112 pages"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Which?", "p": [], "q": "Number of people sharing a $600 rent and each person's share.", "steps": [["double people → half share", ""]], "a": "inverse proportion"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Which?", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m9u11s2t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Litres of petrol bought and total cost are …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "directly proportional", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "inversely proportional", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Treated inverse as direct", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "4 painters take 6 days. How long for 8 painters?", "lines": ["twice as many painters", "so 12 days"], "bad": 1, "why": "More painters means LESS time: 24 painter-days ÷ 8 = 3 days.", "fix": [["4 × 6 = 24", ""], ["24 ÷ 8 = 3 days", ""]], "id": "m9u11s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Using the direct method for an inverse situation", "p": ["Ask whether the answer should go up or down."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Project managers plan staff and time with inverse proportion; shops use direct proportion for prices."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Direct: ratio constant; double ↔ double.", "Inverse: product constant; double ↔ halve.", "Unit method for direct; total method for inverse.", "Check that the answer makes sense."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 720, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "11.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s2k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: days for 8 painters?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "11.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s2k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Painter-days?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 24, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "11.2-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s2k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "12 painters: days?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "11.2-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m9u11s2k04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Quick check: speed and time for a fixed journey …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "inverse", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "direct", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 409]], "req": [{"id": "m9u11s2r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "5 pens cost $3.50. Cost of 8 ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5.6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s2r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "2 workers take 9 hours. 3 workers?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m9u11s2r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "At